-- Winch Up :: sweeping 1 October 2026
--
-- READ ONLY. No writes, no DDL. Safe on production.
--
-- WHY THIS DATE. Two migrations from 1 October had never been applied -- 20261001000100 (which
-- adds 'emergency' to app.ad_slot_allowed, the only thing keeping adverts off the emergency
-- guidance pages) and 20261001000200 (the 'tips' post topic). Two adjacent misses is a lost batch,
-- not a coincidence, so the whole day is re-checked here -- including the two that were fixed, so a
-- regression would show.
--
-- The numbering has gaps: 000300, 000400, 000800 and 000900 are absent from the repo. Statement 1
-- is there for exactly that -- a ledger row with no local file would mean something was applied to
-- production that does not exist in the code, which is the one shape this reconciliation could not
-- have caught by counting.

set search_path = public, extensions;

